 { Stronger side's king in front of the pawnsWhen the king and the rook work together to stop the pawns, they usually win. If the stronger side's king achieves a position in front of the pawns, not even the most favourable scenario (except, of course, promotion) can save the game for the defender. The analysis of this position is very simple. } 1. Ke5 Ra1 2. Kd5 Re1 3. d7+ Ke7 $19 { And the pawns are captured. } 
